@node Introduction
@chapter Introduction

@cindex purpose
@value{PROJECT} is a Rust boot splash for Steelbore OS Bravais.  It shows real
boot progress read from systemd, prompts for disk passphrases inside the splash
through the systemd password-agent protocol, and holds the screen until greetd
takes over the virtual terminal.  It is one process started twice: once in the
initrd, where it draws from the first frame simpledrm can give and prompts for
LUKS, and once after switch-root, where it switches to the real
@code{Manager.Progress} figure and holds the last frame until the greeter
claims the VT.  On shutdown it runs a third time.

@cindex fail-open
Fairing is designed to be fail-open.  No boot target requires it, every wait
on an external resource carries a timeout, and a crash leaves the console and
the stock @command{systemd-tty-ask-password-agent} to finish the boot.  The
residual risk is silent wrongness --- a bar that looks right while lying, or a
passphrase mis-forwarded --- which is why the project is assurance Category B
with two subsystems raised to Category A: the password agent
(@code{fairing-askpass}) and the initrd lifecycle unit.

@cindex crates
@cindex workspace
The source is one Cargo workspace of four product crates:

@multitable @columnfractions .25 .55 .2
@headitem Crate @tab Role @tab Category
@item @code{fairing}
@tab Binary: CLI, lifecycle state machine, systemd notify
@tab B
@item @code{fairing-render}
@tab Backend trait with DRM, fbdev and text implementations; frame compositor
@tab B
@item @code{fairing-theme}
@tab Compiled theme format, Nickel contract, @code{theme check} / @code{theme compile}
@tab B
@item @code{fairing-askpass}
@tab systemd ask-password agent: inotify watcher, bounded parser, socket reply, zeroisation
@tab A
@end multitable

@cindex conformance
The project conforms to The Steelbore Standard v2.12 as a Category B project,
tailored; the tailoring register is @file{COMPLIANCE.md} at the repository
root.  This manual carries the two artefacts the Standard places in Texinfo:
the Needs (@pxref{Needs}) and the Requirements (@pxref{Requirements}).  The
Interfaces (ICD, Standard §23) and Dependencies chapters are added at
the G2 design gate.

